1
00:00:32,200 --> 00:00:35,200
The world is changed.

2
00:00:35,300 --> 00:00:38,200
I feel it in the water.

3
00:00:38,900 --> 00:00:41,700
I feel it in the earth.

4
00:00:43,200 --> 00:00:46,100
I smell it in the air.

5
00:00:46,500 --> 00:00:48,300
Much that once was...

6
00:00:48,500 --> 00:00:50,000
...is lost.

7
00:00:50,700 --> 00:00:53,600
For none now live who remember it.

8
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:10,200
It began with the forging
of the Great Rings.

9
00:01:10,200 --> 00:01:16,000
Three were given to the Elves:
Immortal, wisest and fairest of all beings.

10
00:01:17,400 --> 00:01:24,000
Seven to the Dwarf-lords:
Great miners and craftsmen of the mountain halls.

11
00:01:24,400 --> 00:01:25,600
And nine...

12
00:01:25,800 --> 00:01:28,600
...nine rings were gifted
to the race of Men...

13
00:01:28,900 --> 00:01:32,600
... who, above all else, desire power.

14
00:01:33,600 --> 00:01:38,600
For within these rings was bound
the strength and will to govern each race.

15
00:01:40,100 --> 00:01:43,100
But they were all of them deceived.

16
00:01:43,400 --> 00:01:45,400
For another ring was made.

17
00:01:46,200 --> 00:01:49,600
In the land of Mordor,
in the fires of Mount Doom...

18
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:54,300
... the Dark Lord Sauron forged
in secret a Master Ring...

19
00:01:54,500 --> 00:01:56,400
... to control all others.

20
00:01:56,600 --> 00:02:00,400
And into this Ring he poured
his cruelty, his malice...

21
00:02:00,600 --> 00:02:04,600
...and his will to dominate all life.

22
00:02:05,600 --> 00:02:09,300
One Ring to rule them all.

23
00:02:10,100 --> 00:02:11,700
One by one...

24
00:02:11,900 --> 00:02:16,400
... the Free Lands of Middle-earth
fell to the power of the Ring.

25
00:02:16,600 --> 00:02:19,500
But there were some who resisted.

26
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:24,400
A Last Alliance of Men and Elves
marched against the armies of Mordor.

27
00:02:24,600 --> 00:02:29,100
And on the slopes of Mount Doom, they
fought for the freedom of Middle-earth.

28
00:02:58,200 --> 00:03:00,700
Victory was near.

29
00:03:05,200 --> 00:03:06,900
But the power of the Ring...

30
00:03:07,700 --> 00:03:09,100
...could not be undone.

31
00:03:32,700 --> 00:03:34,500
It was in this moment...

32
00:03:34,700 --> 00:03:37,000
... when all hope had faded...

33
00:03:37,200 --> 00:03:41,100
... that Isildur, son of the king,
took up his father's sword.

34
00:04:11,000 --> 00:04:17,200
Sauron, the enemy of the Free Peoples
of Middle-earth, was defeated.

35
00:04:23,800 --> 00:04:25,900
The Ring passed to Isildur...

36
00:04:26,100 --> 00:04:30,100
... who had this one chance
to destroy evil forever.

37
00:04:30,800 --> 00:04:32,800
But the hearts of Men...

38
00:04:33,000 --> 00:04:35,400
...are easily corrupted.

39
00:04:35,700 --> 00:04:40,100
And the Ring of Power
has a will of its own.

40
00:05:04,300 --> 00:05:06,800
It betrayed Isildur...

41
00:05:08,600 --> 00:05:10,900
... to his death.

42
00:05:14,900 --> 00:05:18,600
And some things
that should not have been forgotten...

43
00:05:18,800 --> 00:05:21,000
... were lost.

44
00:05:21,800 --> 00:05:24,000
History became legend...

45
00:05:24,200 --> 00:05:26,100
...legend became myth.

46
00:05:26,300 --> 00:05:29,000
And for
two and a half thousand years...

47
00:05:29,200 --> 00:05:32,800
... the Ring passed
out of all knowledge.

48
00:05:33,400 --> 00:05:36,100
Until, when chance came...

49
00:05:36,700 --> 00:05:39,700
...it ensnared a new bearer.

50
00:05:41,000 --> 00:05:45,600
My precious.

51
00:05:45,900 --> 00:05:48,300
The Ring came to the creature
Gollum...

52
00:05:48,500 --> 00:05:52,200
... who took it deep into the tunnels
of the Misty Mountains.

53
00:05:52,500 --> 00:05:55,300
And there it consumed him.

54
00:05:55,500 --> 00:05:57,400
It came to me.

55
00:05:57,600 --> 00:06:01,900
My own. My love. My own.

56
00:06:02,100 --> 00:06:06,600
My precious.

57
00:06:10,100 --> 00:06:13,400
The Ring brought to Gollum
unnatural long life.

58
00:06:13,600 --> 00:06:17,200
For 500 years it poisoned his mind.

59
00:06:17,400 --> 00:06:21,800
And in the gloom of Gollum's cave,
it waited.

60
00:06:22,000 --> 00:06:25,200
Darkness crept back
into the forests of the world.

61
00:06:25,400 --> 00:06:28,100
Rumor grew of a shadow in the East...

62
00:06:28,300 --> 00:06:31,000
... whispers of a nameless fear.

63
00:06:31,200 --> 00:06:34,400
And the Ring of Power perceived...

64
00:06:34,600 --> 00:06:37,200
...its time had now come.

65
00:06:39,600 --> 00:06:42,100
It abandoned Gollum.

66
00:06:42,800 --> 00:06:47,000
But something happened then
the Ring did not intend.

67
00:06:47,900 --> 00:06:52,300
It was picked up by the most unlikely
creature imaginable.

68
00:06:52,500 --> 00:06:53,500
What's this?

69
00:06:53,700 --> 00:06:55,100
A Hobbit.

70
00:06:55,200 --> 00:06:57,900
Bilbo Baggins of the Shire.

71
00:06:58,100 --> 00:06:59,800
A ring.

72
00:07:00,000 --> 00:07:01,800
Lost!

73
00:07:04,400 --> 00:07:07,700
My precious is lost!

74
00:07:07,900 --> 00:07:10,100
For the time will soon come...

75
00:07:10,400 --> 00:07:15,300
... when Hobbits will shape
the fortunes of all.

76
00:07:19,900 --> 00:07:22,800
The 22nd day of September...

77
00:07:23,000 --> 00:07:26,100
...in the year 1400...

78
00:07:26,300 --> 00:07:28,500
...by Shire-reckoning.

79
00:07:28,600 --> 00:07:34,200
Bag End, Bagshot Row, Hobbiton,
West farthing...

80
00:07:34,400 --> 00:07:36,300
...the Shire...

81
00:07:36,500 --> 00:07:39,200
...Middle-earth.

82
00:07:43,600 --> 00:07:46,800
The Third Age of this world.

83
00:07:58,400 --> 00:08:02,200
"There and Back Again."

84
00:08:02,300 --> 00:08:04,000
A Hobbit's Tale.

85
00:08:04,200 --> 00:08:08,000
By Bilbo Baggins.

86
00:08:12,600 --> 00:08:14,200
Now...

87
00:08:15,000 --> 00:08:16,900
...where to begin?

88
00:08:18,100 --> 00:08:19,100
Ah, yes....

89
00:08:23,400 --> 00:08:25,200
"Concerning...

90
00:08:26,300 --> 00:08:27,800
...Hobbits."

91
00:08:28,900 --> 00:08:32,300
Hobbits have been living and farming
in the four Farthings of the Shire...

92
00:08:32,400 --> 00:08:34,400
...for many hundreds of years...

93
00:08:34,500 --> 00:08:37,400
...quite content to ignore
and be ignored...

94
00:08:37,600 --> 00:08:40,600
...by the world of the Big Folk.

95
00:08:41,000 --> 00:08:46,400
Middle-earth being, after all,
full of strange creatures beyond count...

96
00:08:46,500 --> 00:08:49,600
...Hobbits must seem
of little importance...

97
00:08:49,800 --> 00:08:53,600
...being neither renowned
as great warriors...

98
00:08:53,800 --> 00:08:57,800
...nor counted among the very wise.

99
00:09:02,000 --> 00:09:04,900
Frodo! Someone at the door.

100
00:09:06,000 --> 00:09:08,500
In fact, it has been remarked by some...

101
00:09:08,700 --> 00:09:12,900
... that Hobbits' only real passion
is for food.

102
00:09:13,300 --> 00:09:15,400
A rather unfair observation...

103
00:09:15,600 --> 00:09:19,000
...as we have also developed a keen
interest in the brewing of ales...

104
00:09:19,500 --> 00:09:22,100
...and the smoking of pipe-weed.

105
00:09:22,600 --> 00:09:25,300
But where our hearts truly lie...

106
00:09:25,500 --> 00:09:27,500
...is in peace and quiet...

107
00:09:28,200 --> 00:09:30,200
...and good, tilled earth.

108
00:09:30,400 --> 00:09:35,400
For all Hobbits share a love
of things that grow.

109
00:09:38,400 --> 00:09:42,600
And, yes, no doubt to others,
our ways seem quaint.

110
00:09:42,800 --> 00:09:47,800
But today of all days,

111
00:09:48,400 --> 00:09:54,100
It is no bad thing
to celebrate a simple life.

112
00:09:58,100 --> 00:10:01,200
Frodo, the door!

113
00:10:04,800 --> 00:10:06,700
Sticklebacks. Where is that boy?

114
00:10:06,800 --> 00:10:08,500
Frodo!

115
00:10:14,000 --> 00:10:17,400
Down from the door where it began

116
00:10:22,000 --> 00:10:25,600
And I must follow if I can

117
00:10:26,600 --> 00:10:30,600
The road goes ever on and on

118
00:10:30,800 --> 00:10:34,000
Down from the door where it began

119
00:10:34,300 --> 00:10:39,000
Now far ahead the road has gone

120
00:10:39,700 --> 00:10:43,300
-And I must follow if I can
-You're late.

121
00:10:46,400 --> 00:10:50,100
A wizard is never late, Frodo Baggins.

122
00:10:50,800 --> 00:10:55,300
Nor is he early. He arrives
precisely when he means to.

123
00:11:06,200 --> 00:11:09,100
It's wonderful to see you, Gandalf!

124
00:11:12,800 --> 00:11:16,400
You didn't think I'd miss
your Uncle Bilbos birthday?

125
00:11:18,000 --> 00:11:20,100
How is the old rascal?

126
00:11:20,600 --> 00:11:24,000
I hear it's going to be a party
of special magnificence.

127
00:11:24,200 --> 00:11:26,500
You know Bilbo.
He's got the whole piece in an uproar.

128
00:11:26,700 --> 00:11:28,600
Well, that should please him.

129
00:11:28,700 --> 00:11:30,500
Half the Shire's been invited.

130
00:11:30,800 --> 00:11:33,300
And the rest of them are turning up
anyway.

131
00:11:36,300 --> 00:11:39,500
And so life in the Shire goes on...

132
00:11:39,700 --> 00:11:42,600
... very much as it has
this past Age...

133
00:11:42,800 --> 00:11:48,100
...full of its own comings and goings,
with change coming slowly.

134
00:11:48,200 --> 00:11:50,100
If it comes at all.

135
00:11:51,300 --> 00:11:54,600
For things are made to endure
in the Shire...

136
00:11:54,800 --> 00:11:58,100
...passing from one generation
to the next.

137
00:11:58,500 --> 00:12:03,300
There's always been a Baggins
living here under the Hill...

138
00:12:03,500 --> 00:12:04,800
...in Bag End.

139
00:12:07,400 --> 00:12:10,100
And there always will be.

140
00:12:10,800 --> 00:12:14,000
To tell you the truth,
Bilbo's been a bit odd lateIy.

141
00:12:15,200 --> 00:12:17,400
I mean, more than usual.

142
00:12:18,400 --> 00:12:20,200
He's taken to locking himself
in his study.

143
00:12:21,700 --> 00:12:25,700
He spends hours poring over old maps
when he thinks I'm not looking.

144
00:12:37,900 --> 00:12:39,500
Where's it gone?

145
00:13:05,000 --> 00:13:07,200
He's up to something.

146
00:13:15,000 --> 00:13:17,400
-All right, then. Keep your secrets.
-What?

147
00:13:17,600 --> 00:13:19,200
But I know you have something
to do with it.

148
00:13:19,500 --> 00:13:20,500
Good gracious me.

149
00:13:20,900 --> 00:13:23,500
Before you came along, we Bagginses
were very well thought of.

150
00:13:23,800 --> 00:13:24,600
Indeed.

151
00:13:24,900 --> 00:13:27,000
Never had any adventures
or did anything unexpected.

152
00:13:27,600 --> 00:13:33,200
If you're referring to the incident
with the dragon, I was barely involved.

153
00:13:33,400 --> 00:13:36,900
All I did was give your uncle
a little nudge out of the door.

154
00:13:37,000 --> 00:13:41,000
Whatever you did, you've been officially
labeled a disturber of the peace.

155
00:13:41,400 --> 00:13:43,200
Oh, really?

156
00:13:48,600 --> 00:13:50,500
Gandalf! Gandalf!

157
00:13:56,400 --> 00:13:57,600
Fireworks, Gandalf!

158
00:14:00,500 --> 00:14:03,000
-Gandalf!
-Fireworks, Gandalf!

159
00:14:21,100 --> 00:14:22,100
Gandalf?

160
00:14:22,700 --> 00:14:26,600
-I'm glad you're back.
-So am I, dear boy.

161
00:14:30,800 --> 00:14:32,600
So am I.

162
00:15:03,100 --> 00:15:04,500
No, thank you!

163
00:15:04,700 --> 00:15:08,400
We don't want any more visitors,
well-wishers or distant relations!

164
00:15:08,700 --> 00:15:12,000
And what about very old friends?

165
00:15:15,100 --> 00:15:16,700
Gandalf?

166
00:15:17,300 --> 00:15:20,600
-Bilbo Baggins.
-My dear Gandalf!

167
00:15:20,900 --> 00:15:25,800
Good to see you. 111 years old!
Who would believe it?

168
00:15:27,500 --> 00:15:29,400
You haven't aged a day.

169
00:15:35,800 --> 00:15:37,700
Come on, come in!

170
00:15:37,900 --> 00:15:40,200
Welcome, welcome.

171
00:15:41,300 --> 00:15:43,700
Oh, here we are.

172
00:15:45,300 --> 00:15:47,700
Tea? Or maybe something
a littIe stronger?

173
00:15:47,800 --> 00:15:51,500
I've got a few bottles
of the Old Winyard left. 1296.

174
00:15:51,700 --> 00:15:55,500
Very good year. Almost as old as I am.

175
00:15:56,700 --> 00:16:01,000
It was laid down by my father.
What say we open one, eh?

176
00:16:01,200 --> 00:16:03,700
Just tea, thank you.

177
00:16:09,900 --> 00:16:11,400
I was expecting you sometime
last week.

178
00:16:11,600 --> 00:16:14,800
Not that it matters. You come and go as
you please. Always have and always will.

179
00:16:15,000 --> 00:16:20,000
You caught me a bit unprepared. We've only
got cold chicken and a bit of pickle....

180
00:16:20,200 --> 00:16:23,400
There's some cheese here.
No, that won't do.

181
00:16:23,600 --> 00:16:27,400
We've got raspberry jam,
an apple tart....

182
00:16:28,000 --> 00:16:31,900
But not much for afters.
Oh, no, we're all right.

183
00:16:32,100 --> 00:16:34,800
I've just found some sponge cake.

184
00:16:37,600 --> 00:16:38,800
I could make you some eggs
if you'd--

185
00:16:42,500 --> 00:16:45,100
-Just tea, thank you.
-Oh, right.

186
00:16:46,100 --> 00:16:48,300
-You don't mind if I eat, do you?
-No, not at all.

187
00:16:49,400 --> 00:16:51,200
Bilbo! Bilbo Baggins!

188
00:16:51,400 --> 00:16:52,900
I'm not at home!

189
00:16:58,700 --> 00:17:01,200
It's the Sackville-Bagginses.

190
00:17:01,400 --> 00:17:03,400
-I know you're in there!
-They're after the house.

191
00:17:04,000 --> 00:17:06,400
They've never forgiven me
for living this long.

192
00:17:06,600 --> 00:17:09,300
I've got to get away from these confounded
relatives, hanging on the bell all day...

193
00:17:09,400 --> 00:17:11,300
...never giving me a moment's peace.

194
00:17:12,000 --> 00:17:15,400
I want to see mountains again.
Mountains, Gandalf!

195
00:17:15,600 --> 00:17:20,000
And then find somewhere quiet
where I can finish my book. Oh, tea.

196
00:17:20,100 --> 00:17:23,900
-So you mean to go through with your plan?
-Yes, yes. It's all in hand.

197
00:17:24,100 --> 00:17:26,200
All the arrangements are made.

198
00:17:28,300 --> 00:17:29,700
Oh, thank you.

199
00:17:30,400 --> 00:17:32,400
Frodo suspects something.

200
00:17:32,600 --> 00:17:35,000
Of course he does. He's a Baggins...

201
00:17:35,200 --> 00:17:37,700
...not some blockheaded Bracegirdle
from Hardbottle.

202
00:17:38,200 --> 00:17:40,900
You will tell him, won't you?

203
00:17:41,700 --> 00:17:43,700
-Yes, yes.
-He's very fond of you.

204
00:17:45,800 --> 00:17:47,300
I know.

205
00:17:49,500 --> 00:17:52,800
He'd probably come with me
if I asked him.

206
00:17:53,400 --> 00:17:56,600
I think in his heart, Frodo's
still in love with the Shire.

207
00:17:58,100 --> 00:18:00,400
The woods, the fields.

208
00:18:00,600 --> 00:18:02,800
Little rivers.

209
00:18:07,100 --> 00:18:09,700
I am old, Gandalf.

210
00:18:11,000 --> 00:18:16,000
I know I don't look it, but I'm
beginning to feel it in my heart.

211
00:18:18,100 --> 00:18:20,600
I feel thin.

212
00:18:20,700 --> 00:18:22,400
Sort of stretched...

213
00:18:23,600 --> 00:18:26,800
...like butter scraped
over too much bread.

214
00:18:27,000 --> 00:18:31,300
I need a holiday. A very long holiday.

215
00:18:31,500 --> 00:18:34,600
And I don't expect I shall return.

216
00:18:36,700 --> 00:18:39,800
In fact, I mean not to.

217
00:18:42,300 --> 00:18:46,200
Old Toby. The finest weed
in the Southfarthing.

218
00:19:02,900 --> 00:19:05,400
Gandalf, my old friend...

219
00:19:05,500 --> 00:19:08,200
...this will be a night to remember.

220
00:19:30,100 --> 00:19:31,200
Hello, hello.

221
00:19:31,400 --> 00:19:35,300
Fatty Bolger. Lovely to see you.
Welcome, welcome.

222
00:19:36,300 --> 00:19:38,700
Go on, Sam. Ask Rosie for a dance.

223
00:19:41,200 --> 00:19:44,600
-I think I'll just have another ale.
-Oh, no, you don't.

224
00:19:45,600 --> 00:19:47,400
Go on!

225
00:19:57,100 --> 00:19:58,800
So there I was...

226
00:19:59,000 --> 00:20:03,000
...at the mercy
of three monstrous trolls.

227
00:20:03,100 --> 00:20:05,000
And they were all arguing
amongst themselves...

228
00:20:05,200 --> 00:20:07,500
...about how they were
going to cook us.

229
00:20:07,700 --> 00:20:12,600
Whether it be turned on a spit, or to sit
on us one by one, squash us into jelly.

230
00:20:13,500 --> 00:20:16,900
They spent so much time arguing
the whithertos and the whyfors...

231
00:20:17,100 --> 00:20:20,600
...that the sun's first light
crept over the top of the trees...

232
00:20:21,500 --> 00:20:23,900
...and turned them all to stone!

233
00:20:29,000 --> 00:20:30,300
Quickly.

234
00:20:34,300 --> 00:20:36,300
Up they go!

235
00:20:39,000 --> 00:20:40,200
No, the big one.

236
00:20:49,000 --> 00:20:51,800
Mrs. Bracegirdle, how nice to see you.
Welcome, welcome.

237
00:20:51,900 --> 00:20:53,800
Are all these children yours?

238
00:20:53,900 --> 00:20:56,800
Good gracious,
you have been productive.

239
00:20:58,700 --> 00:21:00,000
Bilbo?

240
00:21:01,600 --> 00:21:03,300
Sackville-Bagginses!

241
00:21:03,500 --> 00:21:04,500
Quickly, hide!

242
00:21:14,000 --> 00:21:16,100
Thank you, my boy.

243
00:21:17,600 --> 00:21:19,800
You're a good lad, Frodo.

244
00:21:21,000 --> 00:21:23,700
I'm very selfish, you know.

245
00:21:24,100 --> 00:21:27,500
Yes, I am. Very selfish.

246
00:21:27,800 --> 00:21:29,900
I don't know why I took you in after
your mother and father died...

247
00:21:30,100 --> 00:21:31,500
...but it wasn't out of charity.

248
00:21:32,100 --> 00:21:33,400
I think it was because...

249
00:21:33,600 --> 00:21:35,800
...of all my numerous relations...

250
00:21:36,100 --> 00:21:39,500
...you were the one Baggins
that showed real spirit.

251
00:21:39,800 --> 00:21:41,500
Bilbo, have you been
at the Gaffer's home brew?

252
00:21:41,700 --> 00:21:43,300
No.

253
00:21:43,600 --> 00:21:46,100
Well, yes, but that's not the point.

254
00:21:46,300 --> 00:21:49,400
The point is, Frodo...

255
00:21:52,400 --> 00:21:54,300
...you'll be all right.

256
00:21:57,600 --> 00:21:59,500
-Done!
-You're supposed to stick it in the ground.

257
00:21:59,700 --> 00:22:01,200
-It is in the ground.
-Outside!

258
00:22:01,300 --> 00:22:02,800
This was your idea.

259
00:22:18,000 --> 00:22:19,500
Bilbo.

260
00:22:20,500 --> 00:22:23,200
Bilbo, watch out for the dragon!

261
00:22:23,400 --> 00:22:26,600
Nonsense. There hasn't been a dragon
in these parts for a thousand years.

262
00:22:39,600 --> 00:22:43,000
-That was good.
-Let's get another one.

263
00:22:44,300 --> 00:22:48,600
Meriadoc Brandybuck and Peregrin Took.

264
00:22:48,800 --> 00:22:50,600
I might've known.

265
00:22:56,200 --> 00:22:58,200
Speech, Bilbo!

266
00:22:59,100 --> 00:23:00,400
Speech!

267
00:23:00,500 --> 00:23:01,500
Speech!

268
00:23:06,600 --> 00:23:08,700
My dear Bagginses and Boffins...

269
00:23:09,500 --> 00:23:11,600
...Tooks and Brandybucks...

270
00:23:11,800 --> 00:23:14,200
...Grubbs, Chubbs...

271
00:23:14,400 --> 00:23:15,300
...Hornblowers...

272
00:23:16,500 --> 00:23:18,000
...Bolgers...

273
00:23:18,400 --> 00:23:19,900
...Bracegirdles...

274
00:23:20,100 --> 00:23:22,600
-...and Proudfoots.
-Proudfeet!

275
00:23:24,700 --> 00:23:27,800
Today is my 111th birthday!

276
00:23:29,500 --> 00:23:31,000
Happy birthday!

277
00:23:31,200 --> 00:23:35,300
But alas, eleventh-one years is
far too short a time to live among...

278
00:23:35,400 --> 00:23:38,200
...such excellent
and admirable Hobbits.

279
00:23:39,100 --> 00:23:41,700
I don't know half of you
half as well as I should like...

280
00:23:42,000 --> 00:23:46,400
...and I like less than half of you
half as well as you deserve.

281
00:23:55,900 --> 00:23:58,200
I have things to do.

282
00:24:04,300 --> 00:24:06,400
I've put this off far too long.

283
00:24:10,000 --> 00:24:13,800
I regret to announce this is the end!

284
00:24:15,000 --> 00:24:16,100
I'm going now.

285
00:24:17,200 --> 00:24:19,900
I bid you all a very fond farewell.

286
00:24:22,200 --> 00:24:23,300
Goodbye.

287
00:24:55,200 --> 00:24:58,200
I suppose you think that was terribly clever.

288
00:24:58,400 --> 00:25:01,700
Come on, Gandalf.
Did you see their faces?

289
00:25:01,800 --> 00:25:06,700
There are many magic rings in this world,
and none of them should be used lightly.

290
00:25:06,900 --> 00:25:08,900
It was just a bit of fun.

291
00:25:09,200 --> 00:25:12,700
Oh, you're probably right, as usual.

292
00:25:14,000 --> 00:25:17,400
-You will keep an eye on Frodo, won't you?
-Two eyes.

293
00:25:17,600 --> 00:25:20,200
As often as I can spare them.

294
00:25:20,400 --> 00:25:23,400
-I'm leaving everything to him.
-What about this ring of yours?

295
00:25:23,600 --> 00:25:26,800
-Is that staying too?
-Yes, yes.

296
00:25:27,400 --> 00:25:31,200
It's in an envelope over there
on the mantelpiece.

297
00:25:32,200 --> 00:25:35,000
No. Wait, it's...

298
00:25:37,400 --> 00:25:40,000
...here in my pocket.

299
00:25:44,300 --> 00:25:47,600
Isn't that--? Isn't that odd, now?

300
00:25:49,200 --> 00:25:52,500
Yet, after all, why not?

301
00:25:54,000 --> 00:25:58,700
-Why shouldnt I keep it?
-I think you should leave the ring behind.

302
00:25:59,100 --> 00:26:01,200
Is that so hard?

303
00:26:01,400 --> 00:26:02,600
Well, no.

304
00:26:04,900 --> 00:26:06,400
And yes.

305
00:26:08,300 --> 00:26:11,200
Now it comes to it,
I don't feel like parting with it.

306
00:26:11,400 --> 00:26:13,100
It's mine. I found it! It came to me!

307
00:26:13,300 --> 00:26:17,400
-There's no need to get angry.
-Well, if I'm angry, it's your fault!

308
00:26:17,800 --> 00:26:19,500
It's mine.

309
00:26:20,700 --> 00:26:23,100
My own.

310
00:26:23,400 --> 00:26:27,300
-My precious.
-Precious?

311
00:26:27,400 --> 00:26:30,200
It's been called that before,
but not by you.

312
00:26:30,400 --> 00:26:32,900
What business is it of yours
what I do with my own things?

313
00:26:33,100 --> 00:26:35,700
I think you've had that ring
quite long enough.

314
00:26:35,900 --> 00:26:38,600
-You want it for yourself!
-Bilbo Baggins!

315
00:26:38,800 --> 00:26:42,900
Do not take me for some conjurer
of cheap tricks.

316
00:26:43,100 --> 00:26:46,600
I am not trying to rob you.

317
00:26:51,400 --> 00:26:53,100
I'm trying to help you.

318
00:27:01,200 --> 00:27:04,400
All your long years,
we've been friends.

319
00:27:04,800 --> 00:27:06,800
Trust me as you once did.

320
00:27:08,600 --> 00:27:10,400
Let it go.

321
00:27:11,400 --> 00:27:13,800
You're right, Gandalf.

322
00:27:15,800 --> 00:27:18,400
The ring must go to Frodo.

323
00:27:19,700 --> 00:27:22,500
It's late. The road is long.

324
00:27:22,700 --> 00:27:25,100
Yes, it is time.

325
00:27:27,700 --> 00:27:32,600
Bilbo, the ring is still in your pocket.

326
00:28:05,900 --> 00:28:08,800
I've thought up an ending for my book:

327
00:28:10,400 --> 00:28:15,200
"And he lived happily ever after
to the end of his days."

328
00:28:15,400 --> 00:28:18,600
And I'm sure you will, my dear friend.

329
00:28:19,600 --> 00:28:21,000
Goodbye, Gandalf.

330
00:28:23,400 --> 00:28:26,200
Goodbye, dear Bilbo.

331
00:28:33,700 --> 00:28:37,700
The road goes ever on and on

332
00:28:40,200 --> 00:28:42,500
Until our next meeting.

333
00:29:08,700 --> 00:29:12,200
It's mine. My own.

334
00:29:12,400 --> 00:29:15,700
My precious.

335
00:29:16,000 --> 00:29:18,800
Riddles in the dark.

336
00:29:19,000 --> 00:29:20,400
Bilbo!

337
00:29:20,500 --> 00:29:22,000
Bilbo!

338
00:29:25,500 --> 00:29:28,300
My precious.

339
00:29:29,800 --> 00:29:32,000
Precious.

340
00:29:32,200 --> 00:29:34,600
He's gone, hasn't he?

341
00:29:37,200 --> 00:29:40,200
He talked for so long about leaving...

342
00:29:40,400 --> 00:29:43,000
...I didn't think he'd really do it.

343
00:29:47,300 --> 00:29:49,100
Gandalf?

344
00:29:57,000 --> 00:29:58,600
Bilbo's ring.

345
00:29:59,000 --> 00:30:01,200
He's gone to stay with the Elves.

346
00:30:01,400 --> 00:30:04,400
He's left you Bag End.

347
00:30:07,900 --> 00:30:10,300
Along with all his possessions.

348
00:30:10,500 --> 00:30:13,300
The ring is yours now.

349
00:30:15,800 --> 00:30:19,100
-Put it somewhere out of sight.
-Where are you going?

350
00:30:19,300 --> 00:30:21,500
-There are some things that I must see to.
-What things?

351
00:30:21,600 --> 00:30:25,700
-Questions. Questions that need answering.
-You've only just arrived.

352
00:30:26,600 --> 00:30:29,100
I don't understand.

353
00:30:32,300 --> 00:30:33,300
Neither do I.

354
00:30:36,400 --> 00:30:38,600
Keep it secret.

355
00:30:38,800 --> 00:30:40,500
Keep it safe.

356
00:31:14,100 --> 00:31:16,100
Shire!

357
00:31:16,400 --> 00:31:19,400
Baggins!

358
00:32:06,000 --> 00:32:08,800
"The year 3434 of the Second Age.

359
00:32:09,000 --> 00:32:13,200
Here follows the account of Isildur,
High King of Gondor...

360
00:32:13,400 --> 00:32:16,900
...and the finding
of the Ring of Power."

361
00:32:20,300 --> 00:32:22,000
"It has come to me.

362
00:32:22,200 --> 00:32:25,600
The One Ring. It shall be
an heirloom of my kingdom.

363
00:32:25,800 --> 00:32:29,000
All those who follow in my bloodline
shall be bound to its fate...

364
00:32:29,200 --> 00:32:32,900
...for I will risk
no hurt to the Ring.

365
00:32:33,100 --> 00:32:35,400
It is precious to me...

366
00:32:36,300 --> 00:32:38,800
... though I buy it with great pain.

367
00:32:41,800 --> 00:32:45,900
The markings upon the band
begin to fade.

368
00:32:46,200 --> 00:32:50,700
The writing, which at first was as clear
as red flame, has all but disappeared.

369
00:32:50,900 --> 00:32:54,800
A secret now
that only fire can tell."

370
00:33:10,600 --> 00:33:13,500
Shire.

371
00:33:13,700 --> 00:33:15,600
Baggins.

372
00:33:16,100 --> 00:33:19,900
There's no Bagginses around here.
They're all up in Hobbiton.

373
00:33:21,600 --> 00:33:23,000
That way.

374
00:33:28,800 --> 00:33:30,900
To heal my heart and drown my woe

375
00:33:31,100 --> 00:33:33,300
Rain may fall and wind may blow

376
00:33:33,500 --> 00:33:35,400
But there still be

377
00:33:35,500 --> 00:33:36,900
Many miles to go

378
00:33:37,100 --> 00:33:38,900
Sweet is the sound of the pouring rain

379
00:33:39,100 --> 00:33:41,200
And the stream that falls
From hill to plain

380
00:33:41,400 --> 00:33:43,200
Better than rain or rippling brook

381
00:33:43,400 --> 00:33:45,600
Is a mug of beer inside this Took

382
00:33:49,000 --> 00:33:51,600
There's been some strange folk
crossing the Shire.

383
00:33:52,100 --> 00:33:55,800
Dwarves and others of a less
than savory nature.

384
00:33:56,200 --> 00:33:57,600
War is brewing.

385
00:33:58,200 --> 00:34:00,900
The mountains are fair teeming
with goblins.

386
00:34:01,200 --> 00:34:03,600
Far-off tales and childrens stories,
that's all that is.

387
00:34:03,800 --> 00:34:08,100
You're beginning to sound like that old
Bilbo Baggins. Cracked, he was.

388
00:34:08,300 --> 00:34:11,200
Young Mr. Frodo here,
he's cracking.

389
00:34:11,400 --> 00:34:12,700
And proud of it.

390
00:34:12,900 --> 00:34:15,100
-Cheers, Gaffer.
-Cheers.

391
00:34:15,200 --> 00:34:19,200
It's none of our concern what goes on
beyond our borders.

392
00:34:19,400 --> 00:34:23,500
Keep your nose out of trouble,
and no trouble'll come to you.

393
00:34:26,700 --> 00:34:28,800
-Good night, lads.
-Good night.

394
00:34:29,000 --> 00:34:33,300
Good night, sweet maiden
of the golden ale.

395
00:34:33,500 --> 00:34:35,800
Mind who you're sweet-taking.

396
00:34:35,900 --> 00:34:40,200
Don't worry, Sam. Rosie knows an idiot
when she sees one.

397
00:34:41,200 --> 00:34:42,400
Does she?

398
00:34:43,000 --> 00:34:45,900
-Good night, Sam.
-Good night, Mister Frodo.

399
00:35:09,600 --> 00:35:12,000
Is it secret? Is it safe?

400
00:35:20,600 --> 00:35:22,600
What are you doing?

401
00:35:34,700 --> 00:35:37,200
Hold out your hand, Frodo.

402
00:35:37,300 --> 00:35:38,400
It's quite cool.

403
00:35:41,800 --> 00:35:43,500
What can you see?

404
00:35:45,200 --> 00:35:47,500
Can you see anything?

405
00:35:50,100 --> 00:35:51,400
Nothing.

406
00:35:52,100 --> 00:35:54,000
There's nothing.

407
00:35:55,000 --> 00:35:56,400
Wait.

408
00:36:00,400 --> 00:36:02,600
There are markings.

409
00:36:03,900 --> 00:36:07,200
It's some form of Elvish.
I can't read it.

410
00:36:07,400 --> 00:36:09,900
There are few who can.

411
00:36:10,400 --> 00:36:15,100
The language is that of Mordor,
which I will not utter here.

412
00:36:15,700 --> 00:36:16,700
Mordor!

413
00:36:17,000 --> 00:36:18,900
In the common tongue, it says:

414
00:36:19,100 --> 00:36:22,400
"One Ring to rule them all...

415
00:36:22,600 --> 00:36:24,900
...One Ring to find them...

416
00:36:25,100 --> 00:36:27,200
...One Ring to bring them all...

417
00:36:27,400 --> 00:36:30,300
...and in the darkness bind them."

418
00:36:31,900 --> 00:36:33,800
This is the One Ring...

419
00:36:34,100 --> 00:36:39,100
...forged by the Dark Lord Sauron
in the fires of Mount Doom.

420
00:36:39,300 --> 00:36:43,200
Taken by IsiIdur
from the hand of Sauron himself.

421
00:36:43,900 --> 00:36:46,400
Bilbo found it.

422
00:36:46,800 --> 00:36:48,700
-In Gollum's cave.
-Yes.

423
00:36:48,900 --> 00:36:53,200
For 60 years, the Ring lay quiet
in Bilbo's keeping...

424
00:36:53,400 --> 00:36:56,700
...prolonging his life,
delaying old age.

425
00:36:57,300 --> 00:37:01,500
But no longer, Frodo.
Evil is stirring in Mordor.

426
00:37:01,700 --> 00:37:04,000
The Ring has awoken.

427
00:37:04,200 --> 00:37:06,900
It's heard its master's call.

428
00:37:07,100 --> 00:37:10,800
But he was destroyed.
Sauron was destroyed.

429
00:37:16,300 --> 00:37:18,300
No, Frodo.

430
00:37:19,200 --> 00:37:22,400
The spirit of Sauron endured.

431
00:37:22,600 --> 00:37:27,600
His life force is bound to the Ring,
and the Ring survived.

432
00:37:27,900 --> 00:37:30,000
Sauron has returned.

433
00:37:30,900 --> 00:37:32,900
His Orcs have multiplied.

434
00:37:33,100 --> 00:37:37,000
His fortress at Barad-dur
is rebuilt in the land of Mordor.

435
00:37:37,200 --> 00:37:41,700
Sauron needs only this Ring to cover
all the lands in a second darkness.

436
00:37:42,000 --> 00:37:43,900
He is seeking it.

437
00:37:44,100 --> 00:37:47,800
Seeking it. All his thought
is bent on it.

438
00:37:48,000 --> 00:37:50,600
For the Ring yearns above all else...

439
00:37:50,800 --> 00:37:54,100
...to return to the hand
of its master.

440
00:37:54,300 --> 00:37:56,000
They are one...

441
00:37:56,200 --> 00:37:59,200
...the Ring and the Dark Lord.

442
00:37:59,400 --> 00:38:00,400
Frodo...

443
00:38:00,900 --> 00:38:02,700
...he must never find it.

444
00:38:02,900 --> 00:38:03,900
All right.

445
00:38:04,200 --> 00:38:08,400
We put it away. We keep it hidden.
We never speak of it again.

446
00:38:08,500 --> 00:38:11,100
No one knows it's here, do they?

447
00:38:16,500 --> 00:38:17,700
Do they, Gandalf?

448
00:38:18,700 --> 00:38:22,000
There is one other who knew
that Bilbo had the Ring.

449
00:38:23,100 --> 00:38:26,000
I looked everywhere
for the creature Gollum.

450
00:38:26,200 --> 00:38:28,300
But the enemy found him first.

451
00:38:30,000 --> 00:38:32,400
I don't know how long
they tortured him.

452
00:38:32,500 --> 00:38:36,800
But amidst the endless screams and
babbleing they noticed two words.

453
00:38:37,000 --> 00:38:39,100
Shire!

454
00:38:39,200 --> 00:38:40,800
Baggins!

455
00:38:41,000 --> 00:38:42,800
Shire.

456
00:38:42,900 --> 00:38:45,700
Baggins.
But that would Iead them here!

457
00:38:48,300 --> 00:38:49,400
Who goes there?

458
00:38:51,100 --> 00:38:52,200
Take it, Gandalf!

459
00:38:52,600 --> 00:38:53,600
-Take it!
-No, Frodo.

460
00:38:53,800 --> 00:38:56,100
-You must take it!
-You cannot offer me this ring!

461
00:38:56,300 --> 00:38:59,500
-I'm giving it to you!
-Don't tempt me, Frodo!

462
00:39:01,000 --> 00:39:03,100
I dare not take it.

463
00:39:03,400 --> 00:39:05,700
Not even to keep it safe.

464
00:39:06,800 --> 00:39:08,700
Understand, Frodo...

465
00:39:09,400 --> 00:39:12,900
...I would use this Ring
from a desire to do good.

466
00:39:18,100 --> 00:39:23,600
But through me, it would wield a power
too great and terrible to imagine.

467
00:39:24,100 --> 00:39:26,900
-But it cannot stay in the Shire!
-No.

468
00:39:28,700 --> 00:39:30,300
No, it can't.

469
00:39:35,400 --> 00:39:36,700
What must I do?

470
00:39:38,300 --> 00:39:41,700
-You must leave. And leave quickly.
-Where? Where do I go?

471
00:39:41,900 --> 00:39:45,000
Get out of the Shire.
Make for the village of Bree.

472
00:39:45,300 --> 00:39:46,300
Bree.

473
00:39:46,600 --> 00:39:49,200
-What about you?
-I'll be waiting for you...

474
00:39:49,400 --> 00:39:51,800
...at the inn of the Prancing Pony.

475
00:39:52,000 --> 00:39:55,600
-And the Ring will be safe there?
-I don't know, Frodo.

476
00:39:55,700 --> 00:39:57,600
I don't have any answers.

477
00:39:59,100 --> 00:40:04,400
I must see the head of my order. He is
both wise and powerful. Trust me, Frodo.

478
00:40:04,600 --> 00:40:06,600
He'll know what to do.

479
00:40:07,200 --> 00:40:10,000
You'll have to leave the name
of Baggins behind you.

480
00:40:10,200 --> 00:40:12,600
That name is not safe
outside the Shire.

481
00:40:13,200 --> 00:40:16,400
Travel only by day.
And stay off the road.

482
00:40:17,000 --> 00:40:20,000
I can cut across country
easily enough.

483
00:40:22,400 --> 00:40:23,700
My dear Frodo.

484
00:40:24,000 --> 00:40:26,900
Hobbits really are amazing creatures.

485
00:40:27,100 --> 00:40:29,900
You can learn all that there is to
know about their ways in a month.

486
00:40:30,100 --> 00:40:32,400
And yet, after a hundred years...

487
00:40:32,500 --> 00:40:34,500
...they can still surprise you.

488
00:40:36,000 --> 00:40:37,300
Get down.

489
00:40:49,000 --> 00:40:52,400
Confound it all, Samwise Gamgee!
Have you been eavesdropping?

490
00:40:52,600 --> 00:40:56,900
I haven't been dropping no eaves. Honest.
I was cutting the grass under the window.

491
00:40:57,000 --> 00:40:59,400
A little late for trimming the verge,
don't you think?

492
00:40:59,600 --> 00:41:02,300
-I heard raised voices.
-What did you hear? Speak!

493
00:41:02,500 --> 00:41:03,600
Nothing important.

494
00:41:04,100 --> 00:41:08,000
That is, I heard a good deal about a ring,
a Dark Lord and the end of the world but--

495
00:41:08,200 --> 00:41:12,800
Please, Mr. Gandalf, sir, don't hurt me.
Don't turn me into anything unnatural.

496
00:41:13,400 --> 00:41:15,000
No?

497
00:41:16,200 --> 00:41:17,200
Perhaps not.

498
00:41:18,400 --> 00:41:21,700
I've thought of a better use for you.

499
00:41:23,400 --> 00:41:26,300
Come along, Samwise. Keep up.

500
00:41:27,700 --> 00:41:29,800
Be careful, both of you.

501
00:41:30,100 --> 00:41:32,800
The enemy has many spies
in his service:

502
00:41:33,000 --> 00:41:35,800
Birds, beasts.

503
00:41:37,500 --> 00:41:39,200
Is it safe?

504
00:41:40,800 --> 00:41:42,200
Never put it on...

505
00:41:42,400 --> 00:41:45,600
...for the agents of the Dark Lord
will be drawn to its power.

506
00:41:45,800 --> 00:41:47,200
Always remember, Frodo...

507
00:41:47,700 --> 00:41:50,800
...the Ring is trying to get back
to its master.

508
00:41:51,100 --> 00:41:53,200
It wants to be found.

509
00:42:32,100 --> 00:42:34,200
This is it.

510
00:42:34,500 --> 00:42:36,600
This is what?

511
00:42:36,900 --> 00:42:38,800
If I take one more step...

512
00:42:39,400 --> 00:42:43,100
...it'll be the farthest away
from home I've ever been.

513
00:42:47,100 --> 00:42:48,600
Come on, Sam.

514
00:42:56,700 --> 00:42:58,400
Remember what Bilbo used to say:

515
00:42:59,000 --> 00:43:02,600
-"It's a dangerous business, Frodo."
-"Going out your door.

516
00:43:02,800 --> 00:43:07,000
You step onto the road,
and if you don't keep your feet...

517
00:43:07,200 --> 00:43:11,200
... there's no knowing where
you might be swept off to."

518
00:43:24,500 --> 00:43:26,200
Sam.

519
00:43:29,600 --> 00:43:30,600
Wood-elves.

520
00:43:43,800 --> 00:43:47,200
They're going to the harbor
beyond the White Towers.

521
00:43:47,700 --> 00:43:49,400
To the Grey Havens.

522
00:43:50,000 --> 00:43:51,900
They're leaving Middle-earth.

523
00:43:52,100 --> 00:43:54,200
Never to return.

524
00:43:57,000 --> 00:43:59,000
I don't know why...

525
00:43:59,700 --> 00:44:02,000
...it makes me sad.

526
00:44:03,900 --> 00:44:08,400
Everywhere I lie there's a dirty
great root sticking into my back.

527
00:44:09,000 --> 00:44:10,700
Just shut your eyes...

528
00:44:10,900 --> 00:44:13,500
...and imagine you're back
in your own bed...

529
00:44:13,700 --> 00:44:17,500
...with a soft mattress
and a lovely feather pillow.

530
00:44:26,400 --> 00:44:29,000
It's not working, Mr. Frodo.

531
00:44:29,200 --> 00:44:31,900
I'm never going to be able
to sleep out here.

532
00:44:34,200 --> 00:44:36,400
Me neither, Sam.

533
00:45:03,800 --> 00:45:06,700
Smoke rises
from the Mountain of Doom.

534
00:45:06,900 --> 00:45:08,500
The hour grows late.

535
00:45:08,600 --> 00:45:12,000
And Gandalf the Grey
rides to Isengard...

536
00:45:12,300 --> 00:45:14,600
...seeking my counsel.

537
00:45:14,800 --> 00:45:18,600
For that is why you have come,
is it not?

538
00:45:18,800 --> 00:45:20,000
My old friend.

539
00:45:20,300 --> 00:45:21,800
Saruman.

540
00:45:26,400 --> 00:45:29,300
-You are sure of this?
-Beyond any doubt.

541
00:45:30,100 --> 00:45:32,300
So the Ring of Power has been found.

542
00:45:32,500 --> 00:45:35,600
All these long years,
it was in the Shire.

543
00:45:35,800 --> 00:45:38,800
-Under my very nose.
-Yet you did not have the wit to see it.

544
00:45:39,400 --> 00:45:43,600
Your love of the halfling's leaf
has clearly slowed your mind.

545
00:45:44,300 --> 00:45:48,400
But we still have time. Time enough
to counter Sauron if we act quickly.

546
00:45:48,500 --> 00:45:50,000
Time?

547
00:45:50,900 --> 00:45:53,400
What time do you think we have?

548
00:45:53,800 --> 00:45:57,500
Sauron has regained
much of his former strength.

549
00:45:57,700 --> 00:45:59,800
He cannot yet take physical form...

550
00:46:00,000 --> 00:46:02,600
...but his spirit has lost
none of its potency.

551
00:46:03,200 --> 00:46:08,100
Concealed within his fortress,
the Lord of Mordor sees all.

552
00:46:08,600 --> 00:46:14,400
His gaze pierces cloud, shadow,
earth and flesh.

553
00:46:15,800 --> 00:46:18,800
You know of what I speak, Gandalf.

554
00:46:19,700 --> 00:46:24,700
A Great Eye, lidless,
wreathed in flame.

555
00:46:25,600 --> 00:46:27,400
The Eye of Sauron.

556
00:46:27,600 --> 00:46:30,000
He is gathering all evil to him.

557
00:46:30,400 --> 00:46:32,200
Very soon, he'll have summoned
an army...

558
00:46:32,300 --> 00:46:35,100
...great enough for an assault
upon Middle-earth.

559
00:46:35,400 --> 00:46:37,700
You know this?

560
00:46:38,200 --> 00:46:39,700
How?

561
00:46:40,200 --> 00:46:41,800
I have seen it.

562
00:46:42,200 --> 00:46:45,300
A palantir is a dangerous tool,
Saruman.

563
00:46:46,000 --> 00:46:47,400
Why?

564
00:46:47,900 --> 00:46:50,500
Why should we fear to use it?

565
00:46:53,000 --> 00:46:56,800
They are not all accounted for,
the lost Seeing-stones.

566
00:46:57,000 --> 00:47:00,100
We do not know who else
may be watching.

567
00:47:02,600 --> 00:47:05,200
The hour is later than you think.

568
00:47:05,400 --> 00:47:07,600
Sauron's forces are already moving.

569
00:47:09,800 --> 00:47:12,400
The Nine have left Minas Morgul.

570
00:47:12,800 --> 00:47:13,800
The Nine?

571
00:47:13,900 --> 00:47:16,800
They crossed the River Isen
on Midsummer's Eve...

572
00:47:17,000 --> 00:47:19,600
...disguised as riders in black.

573
00:47:19,800 --> 00:47:23,600
-They've reached the Shire?
-They will find the Ring.

574
00:47:25,200 --> 00:47:27,300
And kill the one who carries it.

575
00:47:27,800 --> 00:47:29,200
Frodo!

576
00:47:41,300 --> 00:47:45,500
You did not seriously think that a Hobbit
could contend with the will of Sauron?

577
00:47:46,200 --> 00:47:48,900
There are none who can.

578
00:47:51,300 --> 00:47:54,000
Against the power of Mordor...

579
00:47:54,100 --> 00:47:56,600
...there can be no victory.

580
00:47:58,500 --> 00:48:01,600
We must join with him, Gandalf.

581
00:48:02,800 --> 00:48:05,000
We must join with Sauron.

582
00:48:07,600 --> 00:48:10,200
It would be wise, my friend.

583
00:48:10,600 --> 00:48:12,000
Tell me...

584
00:48:12,200 --> 00:48:13,200
...friend...

585
00:48:14,200 --> 00:48:18,500
...when did Saruman the Wise
abandon reason for madness?

586
00:48:56,400 --> 00:48:58,000
I gave you the chance...

587
00:48:59,100 --> 00:49:01,700
...of aiding me willingly...

588
00:49:01,800 --> 00:49:05,800
...but you have elected
the way of pain!

589
00:49:28,200 --> 00:49:29,600
Mr. Frodo?

590
00:49:30,200 --> 00:49:31,900
Frodo? Frodo!

591
00:49:33,300 --> 00:49:36,400
-I thought I'd lost you.
-What are you taking about?

592
00:49:36,600 --> 00:49:39,400
-It's just something Gandalf said.
-What did he say?

593
00:49:40,200 --> 00:49:43,900
"Don't you lose him, Samwise Gamgee."
And I don't mean to.

594
00:49:44,200 --> 00:49:47,700
Sam, we're still in the Shire.
What could possibly happen?

595
00:49:50,500 --> 00:49:51,500
Frodo.

596
00:49:51,800 --> 00:49:53,900
-Merry, it's Frodo Baggins.
-Hello, Frodo.

597
00:49:54,100 --> 00:49:55,400
Get off him.

598
00:49:55,900 --> 00:49:57,300
Come on, Frodo.

599
00:49:57,500 --> 00:49:59,300
What's the meaning of this?

600
00:49:59,800 --> 00:50:02,700
You've been into Farmer Maggot's crop!

601
00:50:03,800 --> 00:50:05,900
You get back here!

602
00:50:06,800 --> 00:50:08,100
Get out of my field!

603
00:50:08,300 --> 00:50:11,000
You'll know the devil
if I catch up with you!

604
00:50:11,200 --> 00:50:14,000
I don't know why he's so upset.
It's only a couple of carrots.

605
00:50:14,200 --> 00:50:15,300
And some cabbages.

606
00:50:15,400 --> 00:50:18,300
And those three bags of potatoes
that we lifted last week.

607
00:50:18,400 --> 00:50:22,300
-And then the mushrooms the week before.
-Yes, Pippin. My point is...

608
00:50:22,500 --> 00:50:24,600
...he's clearly overreacting.

609
00:50:24,800 --> 00:50:26,200
Run!

610
00:50:39,200 --> 00:50:41,600
Oh, that was close.

611
00:50:42,600 --> 00:50:45,600
I think I've broken something.

612
00:50:46,600 --> 00:50:48,900
Trust a Brandybuck and a Took!

613
00:50:49,000 --> 00:50:52,600
What? That was just a detour.
A short cut.

614
00:50:52,700 --> 00:50:54,900
-Short cut to what?
-Mushrooms!

615
00:51:03,300 --> 00:51:04,700
That's mine.

616
00:51:07,400 --> 00:51:08,900
That's nice, Merry.

617
00:51:09,400 --> 00:51:11,400
Here's a nice one, Sam.

618
00:51:11,600 --> 00:51:14,000
I think we should get off the road.

619
00:51:22,800 --> 00:51:24,100
Get off the road!

620
00:51:24,300 --> 00:51:25,800
Quick!

621
00:51:37,900 --> 00:51:39,400
Be quiet!

622
00:52:43,000 --> 00:52:45,000
What was that?

623
00:53:16,400 --> 00:53:17,800
Anything?

624
00:53:18,500 --> 00:53:19,900
Nothing.

625
00:53:20,600 --> 00:53:22,800
What is going on?

626
00:53:23,300 --> 00:53:27,000
That Black Rider was looking
for something. Or someone.

627
00:53:28,200 --> 00:53:29,600
Frodo?

628
00:53:30,300 --> 00:53:31,300
Get down!

629
00:53:47,600 --> 00:53:49,700
I have to leave the Shire.

630
00:53:50,600 --> 00:53:52,900
Sam and I must get to Bree.

631
00:53:53,000 --> 00:53:54,400
Right.

632
00:53:55,800 --> 00:53:57,900
Bucklebury Ferry. Follow me.

633
00:54:05,900 --> 00:54:07,100
Run!

634
00:54:08,300 --> 00:54:10,200
This way! Follow me!

635
00:54:13,700 --> 00:54:14,600
Run!

636
00:54:27,400 --> 00:54:29,100
Get the rope, Sam!

637
00:54:31,600 --> 00:54:33,100
Frodo!

638
00:54:33,800 --> 00:54:35,200
Run, Frodo!

639
00:54:35,500 --> 00:54:36,500
Go!
-Hurry!

640
00:54:36,700 --> 00:54:39,200
Frodo, come on!

641
00:54:40,100 --> 00:54:42,100
-Come on! Faster!
-Jump!

642
00:54:56,400 --> 00:55:00,400
-How far to the nearest crossing?
-The Brandywine Bridge. 20 miles.

643
00:55:14,400 --> 00:55:15,900
Come on.

644
00:55:26,600 --> 00:55:29,900
-What do you want?
-We're heading for the Prancing Pony.

645
00:55:33,200 --> 00:55:36,000
Hobbits. Four Hobbits!

646
00:55:36,200 --> 00:55:40,000
What's more, out of the Shire by your
talk. What business brings you to Bree?

647
00:55:40,400 --> 00:55:43,400
We wish to stay at the inn.
Our business is our own.

648
00:55:44,500 --> 00:55:46,900
All right, young sir.
I meant no offense.

649
00:55:47,100 --> 00:55:49,500
It's my job to ask questions
after nightfall.

650
00:55:49,700 --> 00:55:52,500
There's talk of strange folk abroad.

651
00:55:52,600 --> 00:55:54,700
Can't be too careful.

652
00:56:13,600 --> 00:56:17,000
Out of the way!
Watch where you're waking.

653
00:56:40,000 --> 00:56:41,500
Excuse me.

654
00:56:42,600 --> 00:56:45,200
Good evening, little masters.
What can I do for you?

655
00:56:45,400 --> 00:56:51,200
If you're looking accommodation, we got
some cozy Hobbit-sized rooms available.

656
00:56:51,400 --> 00:56:55,900
Always proud to cater
to the Little Folk, Mister...?

657
00:56:57,000 --> 00:56:58,900
Underhill. My name's Underhill.

658
00:57:00,100 --> 00:57:02,600
-Underhill, yes.
-We're friends of Gandalf the Grey.

659
00:57:02,700 --> 00:57:05,800
-Can you tell him we've arrived?
-Gandalf?

660
00:57:06,200 --> 00:57:07,800
Gandalf.

661
00:57:08,600 --> 00:57:10,200
Oh, yes...

662
00:57:10,400 --> 00:57:12,400
...I remember. Elderly chap.

663
00:57:12,700 --> 00:57:15,600
Big grey beard, pointy hat.

664
00:57:16,000 --> 00:57:17,700
Not seen him for six months.

665
00:57:24,200 --> 00:57:25,500
What do we do now?

666
00:57:32,400 --> 00:57:33,600
Sam...

667
00:57:33,800 --> 00:57:35,600
...he'll be here. He'll come.

668
00:57:38,200 --> 00:57:40,200
Get out of my way!

669
00:57:42,500 --> 00:57:44,100
What's that?

670
00:57:44,300 --> 00:57:46,700
This, my friend, is a pint.

671
00:57:46,900 --> 00:57:48,400
It comes in pints?

672
00:57:48,800 --> 00:57:52,400
-I'm getting one.
-You got a whole half already!

673
00:57:58,400 --> 00:58:02,100
That fellow's done nothing
but stare at you since we arrived.

674
00:58:05,500 --> 00:58:06,900
Excuse me.

675
00:58:08,700 --> 00:58:11,600
That man in the corner. Who is he?

676
00:58:12,700 --> 00:58:16,900
He's one of them Rangers. They're
dangerous folk, wandering the Wilds.

677
00:58:17,200 --> 00:58:21,500
What his right name is, I've never heard,
but around here he's known as Strider.

678
00:58:23,800 --> 00:58:24,900
Strider.

679
00:58:37,400 --> 00:58:40,500
Baggins.

680
00:58:43,800 --> 00:58:45,300
Baggins.

681
00:58:57,200 --> 00:58:59,300
Baggins? Sure, I know a Baggins.

682
00:59:00,100 --> 00:59:02,800
He's over there. Frodo Baggins.

683
00:59:03,000 --> 00:59:06,000
He's my second cousin,
once removed on his mother's side...

684
00:59:06,100 --> 00:59:08,300
...and my third cousin, twice removed....

685
00:59:12,600 --> 00:59:14,300
-Pippin!
-Steady on, Frodo.

686
00:59:42,600 --> 00:59:45,000
You cannot hide.

687
00:59:47,800 --> 00:59:50,800
I see you.

688
00:59:52,500 --> 00:59:55,100
There is no life...

689
00:59:55,200 --> 00:59:57,400
...in the void.

690
00:59:57,500 --> 00:59:58,900
Only...

691
00:59:59,800 --> 01:00:01,300
...death.

692
01:00:07,000 --> 01:00:11,700
You draw far too much attention
to yourself, "Mr. Underhill."

693
01:00:16,200 --> 01:00:17,200
What do you want?

694
01:00:17,400 --> 01:00:19,300
A little more caution from you.
That is no trinket you carry.

695
01:00:19,700 --> 01:00:22,600
-I carry nothing.
-Indeed.

696
01:00:22,900 --> 01:00:25,300
I can avoid being seen if I wish...

697
01:00:25,500 --> 01:00:29,000
...but to disappear entirely,
that is a rare gift.

698
01:00:29,500 --> 01:00:32,000
-Who are you?
-Are you frightened?

699
01:00:33,200 --> 01:00:34,200
Yes.

700
01:00:34,300 --> 01:00:38,100
Not nearly frightened enough.
I know what hunts you.

701
01:00:42,000 --> 01:00:44,400
Let him go!
Or I'll have you, Longshanks.

702
01:00:46,000 --> 01:00:50,000
You have a stout heart, little Hobbit.
But that will not save you.

703
01:00:50,100 --> 01:00:53,000
You can no longer wait
for the wizard, Frodo.

704
01:00:53,100 --> 01:00:54,100
They're coming.

705
01:02:14,300 --> 01:02:15,700
What are they?

706
01:02:17,800 --> 01:02:19,900
They were once Men.

707
01:02:20,100 --> 01:02:22,200
Great kings of Men.

708
01:02:22,700 --> 01:02:25,700
Then Sauron the Deceiver gave to them
nine rings of power.

709
01:02:26,300 --> 01:02:29,300
Blinded by their greed,
they took them without question.

710
01:02:29,500 --> 01:02:32,700
One by one, falling into darkness.

711
01:02:32,800 --> 01:02:35,200
Now they are slaves to his will.

712
01:02:37,500 --> 01:02:39,100
They are the Nazgul.

713
01:02:39,400 --> 01:02:42,000
Ringwraiths. Neither living nor dead.

714
01:02:42,700 --> 01:02:44,100
At all times they feel...

715
01:02:44,200 --> 01:02:46,100
... the presence of the Ring...

716
01:02:46,300 --> 01:02:50,600
...drawn to the power of the One.
They will never stop hunting you.

717
01:03:00,200 --> 01:03:03,000
-Where are you taking us?
-Into the Wild.

718
01:03:10,900 --> 01:03:14,800
How do we know this Strider
is a friend of Gandalf?

719
01:03:15,000 --> 01:03:17,700
I think a servant of the enemy
would look fairer...

720
01:03:18,000 --> 01:03:21,800
-...and feel fouler.
-He's foul enough.

721
01:03:22,300 --> 01:03:25,100
We have no choice but to trust him.

722
01:03:25,300 --> 01:03:28,600
-But where is he leading us?
-To Rivendell, Master Gamgee.

723
01:03:30,800 --> 01:03:34,000
-To the house of Elrond.
-Did you hear that? Rivendell.

724
01:03:34,600 --> 01:03:37,200
We're going to see the Elves.

725
01:03:58,000 --> 01:04:02,000
-Gentlemen, we do not stop till nightfall.
-What about breakfast?

726
01:04:02,200 --> 01:04:04,800
-You've already had it.
-We've had one, yes.

727
01:04:05,000 --> 01:04:07,100
What about second breakfast?

728
01:04:10,300 --> 01:04:13,400
Don't think he knows
about second breakfast, Pip.

729
01:04:13,600 --> 01:04:18,600
What about elevenses? Luncheon?
Afternoon tea? Dinner? Supper?

730
01:04:18,800 --> 01:04:22,800
-He knows about them, doesn't he?
-I wouldnt count on it.

731
01:04:28,000 --> 01:04:29,600
Pippin!

732
01:04:45,400 --> 01:04:48,700
What do they eat
when they can't get Hobbit?

733
01:05:26,200 --> 01:05:28,300
Who is she?

734
01:05:29,300 --> 01:05:30,900
This woman you sing of.

735
01:05:34,500 --> 01:05:36,500
'Tis the lady of Luthien.

736
01:05:36,900 --> 01:05:41,500
The EIf-maiden who gave her love
to Beren, a mortal.

737
01:05:43,500 --> 01:05:45,500
What happened to her?

738
01:05:47,500 --> 01:05:49,500
She died.

739
01:05:53,500 --> 01:05:55,900
Get some sleep, Frodo.

740
01:06:06,500 --> 01:06:10,500
The power of Isengard
is at your command...

741
01:06:10,500 --> 01:06:14,500
... Sauron, Lord of the Earth.

742
01:06:17,500 --> 01:06:23,500
Build me an army worthy of Mordor.

743
01:06:28,500 --> 01:06:33,500
What orders from Mordor, my lord?
What does the Eye command?

744
01:06:33,500 --> 01:06:35,500
We have work to do.

745
01:07:16,500 --> 01:07:20,500
The trees are strong, my lord.
Their roots go deep.

746
01:07:20,900 --> 01:07:22,900
Rip them all down.

747
01:07:49,500 --> 01:07:51,500
This was the great watchtower
of Amon Sul.

748
01:07:53,500 --> 01:07:55,500
We shall rest here tonight.

749
01:08:07,500 --> 01:08:10,500
These are for you.
Keep them close.

750
01:08:10,900 --> 01:08:13,500
I'm going to have a look around.

751
01:08:15,500 --> 01:08:16,500
Stay here.

752
01:08:19,500 --> 01:08:20,500
My tomato's burst.

753
01:08:21,500 --> 01:08:23,000
Could I have some bacon?

754
01:08:24,200 --> 01:08:25,200
Want a tomato, Sam?

755
01:08:26,500 --> 01:08:30,100
-What are you doing?!
-Tomatoes, sausages, nice crispy bacon.

756
01:08:30,100 --> 01:08:33,800
-We saved some for you, Mr. Frodo.
-Put it out, you fools!

757
01:08:33,800 --> 01:08:35,800
-Put it out!
-That's nice! Ash on my tomatoes!

758
01:08:44,800 --> 01:08:45,800
Go!

759
01:09:37,800 --> 01:09:38,800
Back, you devils!

760
01:10:58,900 --> 01:10:59,800
Frodo!

761
01:11:04,800 --> 01:11:05,800
Oh, Sam.

762
01:11:41,800 --> 01:11:42,800
Strider!

763
01:11:44,800 --> 01:11:49,800
-Help him, Strider.
-He's been stabbed by a Morgul blade.

764
01:11:51,800 --> 01:11:55,800
This is beyond my skill to heal.
He needs Elvish medicine.

765
01:12:00,800 --> 01:12:01,800
Hurry!

766
01:12:01,800 --> 01:12:05,800
We're six days from Rivendell!
He'll never make it!

767
01:12:05,800 --> 01:12:07,800
Hold on, Frodo.

768
01:12:08,400 --> 01:12:09,800
Gandalf!

769
01:14:41,800 --> 01:14:45,800
Look, Frodo. It's Mr. Bilbo's trolls.

770
01:14:46,800 --> 01:14:50,800
Mr. Frodo? He's going cold.

771
01:14:52,800 --> 01:14:53,800
Is he going to die?

772
01:14:54,200 --> 01:14:58,800
He's passing into the Shadow World.
He'll soon become a Wraith like them.

773
01:15:03,800 --> 01:15:07,800
-They're close.
-Sam, do you know the Athelas plant?

774
01:15:07,800 --> 01:15:09,800
-Athelas?
-Kingsfoil.

775
01:15:09,800 --> 01:15:10,800
Kingsfoil, aye, it's a weed.

776
01:15:10,800 --> 01:15:13,800
It may help to slow the poisoning.
Hurry!

777
01:15:27,000 --> 01:15:31,800
What's this?
A Ranger caught off his guard?
